00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.500
Welcome from Cox's Bazar, Bangladesh. Cox's Bazar is widely recognized as the world's longest natural, unbroken sandy sea beach, stretching approximately 120–150 kilometers (75–93 miles) along the Bay of Bengal

00:01:00.002 --> 00:01:30.010
Width: The beach is approximately 200 meters wide at high tide and up to 400 meters wide at low tide. 

00:02:00.003 --> 00:02:30.011
Location: Situated south of Chittagong in the southeastern part of Bangladesh. 
Best Time to Visit: The best time is typically October to March for better weather. 

